sarah thomas joins us now 48 hours later  sarah thomas hello hello hello we  welcome you  tell me this what is it like when dreams  come true  there's no words for it gail i mean  honestly it's just  it i couldn't say that i ever set out to  be a football official but i ended up  falling in love with it i often joke  about  i hated the officials when i was playing  and they hated me  but as you pursue this career and you  fall in love with what you're doing and  to be a part of  such a strong fraternity and they let a  little sister in and i know there's  going to be some more women following me  i read before you started the game on  sunday you said i might get a little  teary-eyed did you  i did in my hotel room did you i did  take us there saturday night  yeah so saturday night my mother had  pinned a little angel on me when i was a  freshman in college and she told me she  said  i may not be there with you um in person  but i'll be there with you in spirit  as you go through this journey of  college and so she found that angel  and she pitted on a little note and said  we're not going to be there with you in  person but we're there with you in  spirit  you pin this on your uniform somewhere  and then i listen to  rise up that song yes andre day yes  oh my just every word from the start  to the end is i have chills now and that  got me emotional because  i would do this a thousand times again  and rise up  into this over and over and that song  just had a lot of meaning and  it just kind of um choked me up sunday  morning sarah  i'm struck by the fact that in many ways  this started for you back in fifth grade  when you were the only girl on the  basketball team in pascagoula  mississippi  my mom's oldest sister jill lupton she  coached the u.s world team in 73 that  went to moscow russia  and the first female coach that ever  coached  collegiately is from mississippi dot  murphy and my aunt coached her but when  i was in fifth grade my aunt looked at  me and she goes  are you gonna play basketball and i said  they don't have a girls team she said go  out for the boys team  so i did let's talk about the actual  game so you're on the field  it's four reps total you're running up  and down the field did you always feel  confident on the field that day did you  feel ever  intimidated or unsure of your calls or  how you'd be treated by the players  listen this wasn't your first game but  it's the super bowl did it feel  differently to you  that particular day not at all gail  we look at the nfl any given sunday and  we treat it as it's our super bowl  and so this game was no different and  the crew that i had the opportunity to  work with and carl sheffer's  leading this crew and sean hockey lee  the crew i was on the entire season  um we prepare all year for this game if  we're given the opportunity to work it  so we were prepared and we were ready  hey sarah you know i i don't know if you  know this but millions of people who  watch football games at home  think they're the best referees  that's true they see everything they got  all the cameras and they know the right  calls  what's it like being on the field  knowing that that's going on in people's  homes  it's amazing the professionalism that  the nfl illustrates  on the field and off the field with  players and coaches and  it's short-lived they'll express their  passion about what what happened and  i'll go back and you know review things  and  review the whole entire game but you  know to all the fans at home  um especially as it gets later into the  game i guess they're probably seeing it  like  double vision or triple vision because  maybe they're into the adult beverages  good point everybody has a great time  and i'm just glad that there are a lot  of fans out there that support the nfl  sarah we have a selfie that your son  took with you  on the field on sunday what did it mean  for your son to see  for your daughter to see you refereeing  the super bowl  yeah both of my sons were there brady  and  ridley that was really that i was with  and then of course bailey was there  them being there i think just  gave me another sense of just calm that  they're there they're safe and  i often say being the first in any of  this  is not what i set out to do but being a  mom first is what i am to do  so having them there and to share this  with me  um it was just unbelievable  sarah why did i love the ponytail so  much yeah i just love seeing that  ponytail  gail don't you just love that blonde  ponytail i love it  you know whenever whenever gerald alston  hired me  he told me that i needed to tuck my hair  to blend in  and wear little to no makeup and i said  gerald you're crossing the line there's  a lot of things i think the good look  for and makeup's one of them  but i understand why he did that so i  wouldn't  immediately be stereotyped that i  shouldn't be out there because i'm a  woman  but as things have progressed it's not  about my hair  anymore gail of course all of us it's  great my aunt is 102 as of yesterday  and she can spot me real easily so  um it's awkward for me to see myself  with the ponytail but like i said when  gerald hired me i wore a ponytail and  i'm like  you knew i was a woman but anyway  it feels a lot better and a lot more  natural with my hair in a ponytail as  the song goes you're a whole lot of  woman sarah thomas you're a badass we  are cheering you on congratulations  thank you  thank you thank you
 

